{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789229520,"nonce":"EhJUk2N1bATlDEqe7YDMVjJs/ug=","message":"Fixed in 85998b9.\n\nEvidence first: a scan of every OInt in the 79-program corpus plus a probe with negative and 32-bit-edge hl.I64 literals found no OInt targeting an I64 register -- Haxe 4.3.6 emits OInt into an Int register followed by OToInt (Int -\u003e I64) every time. So the zext could not be reached from Haxe output. HashLink's store_const sign-extends, and a hand-built program can reach it, so the LLVM tier sign-extends into a wider int slot and both interpreter walkers box the value with from_i64 when the destination register is HI64; the retyped_reads test rewrites TestIntIntoI64's `Int; ToInt` pairs into that shape and runs it on every engine (without the fix the AOT arm printed sum=4294967279 for -17).\n\nAdjacent, reachable from Haxe and fixed in the same commit: ToSFloat/ToUFloat of an I64 register gave NaN in both walkers, and ToDyn of an F32 register handed hlp_make_dyn the f64 bits (printed 0 for -3).","files":null}]}